#4471 is not one issue. The incident page says **one issue, one fix queued**, but the export's
own grouping shows **two causes** in the 412 unique reports. The desk's subject-line triage put
them together; they need separate tickets.

## What the export shows

<SplitTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/yushanwebdev/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/yushanwebdev/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
  }}
/>

## Two tickets

The counts above are computed from the same grouping. One ticket per cause:

- **`parser`** — 379 reports. The shared parser reads every date month-first; eleven tenants write day-first, so a booking for 7 May becomes an invite for 5 July. App and email always use the parser. A booking-v2 form prints `DD/MM/YYYY`, so its input also lands here.
- **`hint`** — 33 reports. Three tenants run booking-v3, whose form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Their people type month-first as the hint says, and the form reads it day-first. The flip goes the other way, and the parser fix does not touch it.

## Why the tags cannot decide

Intake tags are guesses. In these reports, 23 `parser` reports carry the `hint` tag and 15
`hint` reports carry the `parser` tag. The cause comes from the tenant's locale and form, as
`causes.ts` does it, not from `meta.intakeTag`.

## Counts and duplicates

The export holds 427 rows but **412 unique report IDs**. `uniqueById` removes the overlap before
grouping. Every unique report belongs to #4471, so the two tickets cover all 412.

## One-day move

Five reports in the `parser` group read as a one-day move, not a month/day flip: `R-41202`,
`R-41209`, `R-41236`, `R-41344`, `R-41620`. The desk's `desk-notes.json` counts them under
`parser` and footnotes them. They stay in the parser count here; engineering should decide
whether they need their own fix.

## Resolution

The desk closed #4471 on 05 Oct:

- **`parser`** — fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **`hint`** — won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired.

Both tickets are closed. The split still matters: the fix covers the parser group, and the 33
hint reports stop when the form retires.

## What changed

This page replaces the **one issue, one fix queued** note on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471). The
parser ticket is still needed; it is now one of two.

